// This file specifies the knobs for the damage decay system
 
// DecayDelay specifies a damage source's grace period before its damage starts decaying.  Any time a source deals
//  fresh damage, this grace period starts over.  A negative value indicates no damage is valid to decay, 
//  effectively disabling decaying damage.
//
// RegenFactor specifies a bonus or penalty to the health regen used to decay.  A value of 0.5 would mean that
//  only half of the health actually regenerated would be used to decay damage.  A value of 0.0 would disable
//  decaying damage.
//
// FullDiscardDelay specifies a damage source's grace period before its damage is completely discarded.  Any time
//  a source deals damage, this grace period starts over.  A negative value disables this specific discard system.
//
// DiscardDamage specifies the minimum amount of damage tracked for any one source.  This is relative to the
//  target's max health.  0.1 would mean any source that has dealt less than 10% of the target's max health
//  will have the damage discarded during regen.  A value of 0.0 disables this specific discard system.


//	// This config mimics the original system
//	{
//		DecayDelay			-1
//		FullDiscardDelay	-1
//		DiscardDamage		0.0
//		RegenFactor			0.0
//	}


// New config
{
	DecayDelay			20
	FullDiscardDelay	-1
	DiscardDamage		0.001
	RegenFactor			1.0
}